  data:  # bc2a
    kind: invariant  # bc2a
    title: "SCIP local bindings are document-scoped but resolved through one global map, so 329 of 455 local-pointing edges assert a cross-file reference that cannot exist"  # bc2a
    status: violated  # bc2a
    priority: 2  # bc2a
    parent:  # bc2a
    tags:  # bc2a
    - rust  # bc2a
    - analysis_quality  # bc2a
    - multi_fidelity  # bc2a
    isbefore: []  # bc2a
    duplicate_of: []  # bc2a
    not_duplicate_of: []  # bc2a
    pr_ref:  # bc2a
    description: "MEASURED 2026-09-18 at d6174d5df9, two independent runs (mine and a commissioned\nreview), `HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1 hypergumbo survey ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/aardvark-dns`.\n\nTHE DEFECT. SCIP names a function-local binding with a DOCUMENT-SCOPED index:\nthe moniker is literally `local 0`, `local 1`, `local 42`, and the same string\ndenotes a DIFFERENT binding in every file. Proven from the data, not the spec:\n`local 0` carries a Definition-role occurrence in TEN distinct files of this one\ncrate (build.rs, src/backend/mod.rs, src/commands/run.rs, src/commands/version.rs,\nsrc/config/mod.rs, src/dns/coredns.rs, src/error.rs, src/main.rs,\nsrc/server/serve.rs, src/test/test.rs). A symbol cannot be defined ten times in\nten files.\n\ntranslate.py:231-234 then builds ONE map over the WHOLE index, keyed on that raw\nstring:\n\n    id_by_scip_symbol = {\n        (sym.meta or {}).get(\"scip_symbol\"): sym.id\n        for sym in symbols\n        if sym.meta and sym.meta.get(\"scip_symbol\")\n    }\n\nTen document-scoped `local 0` Symbols collapse to one key, and every edge naming\n`local 0` in any file resolves to one arbitrary winner. 669 SCIP Symbols reduce\nto 299 distinct moniker keys; 133 distinct `local N` strings cover 500 local\nSymbols; 367 local Symbols can never be an edge endpoint at all.\n\nTHE HARM, and it is not merely degenerate identity -- the edges are FALSE.\nEach local-pointing edge is sourced from the file-level module namespace of the\nREFERENCING document, so src.path IS the referencing file. For a document-scoped\nlocal, dst.path != src.path is therefore definitionally wrong:\n\n     123 from namespace 'serve'   (src/server/serve.rs)   116 cross-file\n     116 from namespace 'coredns' (src/dns/coredns.rs)     74 cross-file\n      77 from namespace 'config'  (src/config/mod.rs)      39 cross-file\n      53 from namespace 'test'    (src/test/test.rs)       53 cross-file\n      39 from namespace 'backend' (src/backend/mod.rs)      0 cross-file\n      26 from namespace 'error'   (src/error.rs)           26 cross-file\n      13 from namespace 'crate'   (src/lib.rs)             13 cross-file\n       6 from namespace 'run'     (src/commands/run.rs)     6 cross-file\n       2 from namespace 'version' (src/commands/version.rs)  2 cross-file\n    ----\n     455 local-pointing edges, 329 CROSS-FILE\n\n**329 of 455 (72.3%) are provably false. That is 51.6% of all SCIP edges and\n21.2% of all 1550 edges in the artifact.** The remaining 126 are correct only by\ncoincidence -- the map's arbitrary winner happened to sit in the referencing file.\n\nA SECOND-ORDER HARM: all 455 in-edges land on just 133 nodes, so degenerate\nlocals dominate centrality. selection/filters.py:302-331 lists `local` in\nKEY_SYMBOL_KINDS under the comment `# Terraform/HCL`, so is_key_symbol admits\nthem: 447 of the 500 pass that predicate, and SIX of the top-14 highest-in-degree\nnodes in the whole artifact are locals named '0','1','2','3','4','5' in\nsrc/backend/mod.rs -- outranking almost every real function in the sketch's\nattention budget.\n\nWHY IT WAS NEVER SEEN. The backend has no persistent enable (WI-sobig): the gate\nreads one env var and hypergumbo has no config file, so in ordinary use this arm\nnever runs. No CI job and no bakeoff sets it. Five months of false edges behind\na flag nobody can durably turn on. This is the LIVE.md \"measure across\nCONFIGURATIONS, not just repos\" lesson as a live consequence.\n\nFIX SHAPE, and the precedent is in-tree. Fold the document path into the scoped\nkey on BOTH sides -- the hashed moniker (see the sibling row on stable_id) and\ntranslate.py's resolve map -- so `local 0` in serve.rs and `local 0` in error.rs\nare distinct. **WI-titiz is the same failure mode already fixed once**: a TOML\ndependency stable_id hashed only the package name, collapsing the same package\nacross manifests, and the remedy was to fold the declaring manifest path into\nthe hash (make_dependency_stable_id, \"a package declared in N manifests becomes\nN nodes\"). Identical shape, identical cure.\n\nThis would make all 455 edges REAL at zero recall cost, which is why the drop\nproposed in the sibling locals row is a defensible retreat rather than a proof\nthe edges are worthless.\n\nREPRO: HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1 hypergumbo survey <rust repo> --out F, then\nfor each edge whose dst is a kind=\"local\" node, compare src.path to dst.path.\nAny difference is a false edge. Control: the same survey without the env var.\n\nNOT CLAIMED: corpus-wide. One crate carries the measurement; the mechanism is\nstructural (a document-scoped id in a global map) so it generalises by\nconstruction, but the 329 is repo-specific."  # bc2a
    fields:  # bc2a
      statement: "An emitted edge must not assert a reference relationship between two symbols that cannot reference each other; specifically, an edge whose destination is a function-local binding must have both endpoints in the same file, because a SCIP local id is scoped to its document."  # bc2a
      root_cause: "translate.py builds id_by_scip_symbol as a single index-wide dict keyed on the raw SCIP moniker, but a local moniker ('local 0') is document-scoped and recurs in every file, so all occurrences collapse to one arbitrary winner and references resolve to a binding in the wrong file."  # bc2a
